/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 131 0 R
/E (Traditional text prediction systems have relied on statistical N-gram language models, backoff smoothing \(such as Katz or Kneser-Ney smoothing\), and dictionary-matching autocomplete engines. These systems predict the next word by calculating conditional probabilities based on the immediate preceding two or three words. While computationally lightweight, they lack deep contextual understanding, struggle with long-range syntactic dependencies, and fail when encountering out-of- vocabulary or novel phrasings. )
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
